A Discord bot built on [discord-bot-base](https://github.com/mohanz1/discord-bot-base).

## Run it

```bash
uv sync
cp .env.example .env      # set BOT_TOKEN
uv run {{ project_slug }}
```

## Add a command

Drop a module in `src/{{ package_import_name }}/ext/` — it is discovered and loaded
automatically. See `ext/hello.py` for a worked example.

```python
from __future__ import annotations

import discord
from discord import app_commands

from botbase.cog import BaseCog


class Ping(BaseCog):
    @app_commands.command(description="pong")
    async def ping(self, interaction: discord.Interaction) -> None:
        await interaction.response.send_message("pong")


async def setup(bot) -> None:
    await bot.add_cog(Ping(bot))
```
